commit c5eda264d0957c9e0e4f4106dd14e0c17913c38a
Author: RaYYeR220 <egorslavutich@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 12 02:51:28 2026 +0200

    verify: tighten contradicted/stale rules for errored test runs and non-code edits

    An errored test command with no recognised failing summary (e.g. a shell
    error before pytest ever ran) no longer reads as a failed test run: it is
    unknown, and the claim is unverifiable rather than contradicted. Staleness
    now requires an edit to a code file, not any file touched after a passing
    run, so rewriting a data or evidence file no longer flags a true result as
    stale. Updates the flag scene's wording to match. Both changes are built
    from real contradicted/stale verdicts read off a pattern-based scan of
    public sessions.

